# Template for local secrets. This example file is committed — keep real keys OUT.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# YOU NEED **TWO** FILES WITH THE SAME CONTENTS. Both are gitignored.
#
#   .dev.vars    read by the WORKERS runtime (wrangler dev / npm run preview)
#   .env.local   read by NEXT.JS into process.env (npm run dev)
#
# Libraries that read `process.env` — including @clerk/backend — do NOT see
# .dev.vars. Setting only .dev.vars makes Clerk start in "keyless mode" and
# webhook verification fails with "Missing webhook signing secret", even though
# the dev server prints "Using secrets defined in .dev.vars". Copy this file to
# BOTH names:
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#   cp .dev.vars.example .env.local
#
# Production is separate again — Cloudflare reads neither file:
#   npx wrangler secret put CLERK_SECRET_KEY
#   npx wrangler secret put CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET
#   npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Clerk (https://dashboard.clerk.com) ---
# Publishable key is safe to expose to the browser; secret key is not.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<your Clerk publishable key>"
CLERK_SECRET_KEY="<your Clerk secret key>"

# From Clerk Dashboard → Webhooks → your endpoint → Signing Secret.
# Starts with `whsec_`. Without it, webhook verification fails.
CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET="<your Clerk webhook signing secret>"

# --- Resend (https://resend.com/api-keys) ---
RESEND_API_KEY="<your Resend API key>"
# Must be on a domain verified in Resend.
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL="events@yourdomain.com"
